@startuml
!include style.iuml
mainframe class Singleton
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
hide empty members
left to right direction
title Singleton — as built (UML 2.5.1 class diagram)
class ConnectionPool <<singleton>> {
  -{static} instance : ConnectionPool
  -idle : BlockingQueue<Connection>
  -created : AtomicInteger
  -ConnectionPool(url, user, password, maxSize)
  +{static} initialize(url, user, password, maxSize) : ConnectionPool
  +{static} getInstance() : ConnectionPool
  +{static} shutdown() : void
  +acquire() : Connection
  +release(c : Connection) : void
}
class App <<composition root>>
class TransactionManager
class "AbstractOrmDAO<T, ID>" as AbstractOrmDAO
App ..> ConnectionPool : initialize(...)
App ..> TransactionManager : <<create>> with the pool
TransactionManager --> "1" ConnectionPool : acquire / release
AbstractOrmDAO --> "1" TransactionManager : withConnection
note right of ConnectionPool
  Private constructor + synchronized static factory + volatile field.
  initialize() with DIFFERENT settings fails fast (it used to return
  the old pool silently). Discussion: frameworks prefer a DI-managed
  singleton scope to a static accessor.
end note
@enduml
